join Dagger left
join Lizzy right
Dagger: I suppose she's noticed how frequently we've been speaking.
Dagger: How... 
Dagger: ...
Dagger: You affect me, Lizzy.
Lizzy: Dagger...
Lizzy: I’m sorry about how I’ve been treating you.
Dagger: Don’t apologize.
Dagger: I’m the one who should know not to play with your emotions.
Dagger: There’s an unspoken bond between us,
Dagger: You understand me unlike any other.
Lizzy: In your weird way, I think you understand me too.
Dagger: I don’t want to lose that.
Dagger: Even more than I fear your death.
Dagger: I’d rather know you while you’re alive.
Lizzy: That’s oddly sweet.
Dagger: I have my moments.
Lizzy: ...
Lizzy: This isn’t easy for me to say,
Lizzy: but I want to know you too—
